# Server Functions & Auth Enforcement

## Every Server Function MUST Validate Auth

Every server function that reads or writes user data must call `getUser(accessToken)` and verify the result. No exceptions.

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
export async function updateProfile(accessToken: string, data: ProfileUpdate) {
  requireAccessToken(accessToken);
  const supabase = getUserScopedSupabaseClient(accessToken);
  const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser();
  if (!user) throw authRequired();
  // proceed...
}

// ❌ BAD — trusts client-provided userId without auth
export async function updateProfile(userId: string, data: ProfileUpdate) {
  await supabase.from('profiles').update(data).eq('id', userId);
}
```

## Service Role Client Requires Role Assertion

Any code using `getServiceRoleSupabaseClient()` must have a preceding auth + role assertion:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
assertAdminRole(role);
const supabase = getServiceRoleSupabaseClient();

// ❌ BAD — no role check before privileged client
const supabase = getServiceRoleSupabaseClient();
```

## Audit Logging Is Fail-Closed

All destructive admin actions (suspend, delete, role change, session terminate) must log to `admin_actions`. If the log insert fails, the parent operation MUST fail:

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
const { error } = await supabase.from('admin_actions').insert({ ... });
if (error) throw appError('UNKNOWN', 'Audit log failed — operation aborted');

// ❌ BAD — swallows audit failure
const { error } = await supabase.from('admin_actions').insert({ ... });
if (error) console.error('Failed to log'); // silent
```

## RBAC Source of Truth

- Single role authority: `profiles.role`
- JWT claims are derived (not authoritative)
- `user_roles` table is for audit/history only
- Role changes must invalidate client cache immediately via `invalidateRole()`
